1
00:00:00,112 --> 00:00:02,125
Why can't a superpower just walk away from

2
00:00:02,138 --> 00:00:03,038
a war it's losing?

3
00:00:03,462 --> 00:00:06,350
Political scientist Robert Pape says it's because war

4
00:00:06,425 --> 00:00:07,212
isn't chess.

5
00:00:07,625 --> 00:00:08,137
It's roulette.

6
00:00:08,550 --> 00:00:09,212
You bet on red.

7
00:00:09,625 --> 00:00:10,475
It comes up black.

8
00:00:10,888 --> 00:00:12,388
A rational player walks away.

9
00:00:12,812 --> 00:00:14,150
But the gambler doubles down,

10
00:00:14,450 --> 00:00:16,875
then borrows chips and bets even bigger.

11
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:19,950
Pape maps each spin onto the Iran war:

12
00:00:20,362 --> 00:00:21,500
kill the Supreme Leader,

13
00:00:21,900 --> 00:00:23,362
a six week air campaign,

14
00:00:23,750 --> 00:00:24,388
a blockade.

15
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:25,312
Each time,

16
00:00:25,738 --> 00:00:27,500
he says, Iran didn't fold.

17
00:00:27,912 --> 00:00:28,525
And the chips?

18
00:00:28,938 --> 00:00:30,575
Gas prices, lives,

19
00:00:30,650 --> 00:00:31,675
and political support.

20
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:33,325
That's the escalation trap.

21
00:00:33,812 --> 00:00:35,850
Full animated breakdown on my channel.
